{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define MOD 1000000007\n#define N 33\ntypedef long long ll;\nll n, m, bin[66];\nstruct matrix {\n    ll a[N][N];\n    matrix() { memset(a, 0, sizeof(a)); }\n    matrix operator*(const matrix &b) const {\n        matrix c;\n        for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i)\n            for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j)\n                for (int k = 0; k <= m; ++k)\n                    c.a[i][j] = (c.a[i][j] + a[i][k] * b.a[k][j]) % MOD;\n        return c;\n    }\n} ans, P[66][N], S[66][N], A[66][N];\nll read() {\n    ll x = 0, f = 1;\n    char ch = getchar();\n    while (ch < '0' || ch > '9') { if (ch == '-') f = -1; ch = getchar(); }\n    while (ch >= '0' && ch <= '9') { x = x * 10 + ch - '0'; ch = getchar(); }\n    return x * f;\n}\nsigned main() {\n    n = read(); m = read();\n    int len = 0;\n    ll tmp = n;\n    while (tmp) { bin[len++] = tmp % m; tmp /= m; }\n    if (len == 0) len = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= m; ++i) ans.a[0][i] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < len; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= m; ++j) A[i][0].a[j][j] = 1;\n        if (i == 0) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                A[i][j].a[m][m] = 1;\n                for (int k = 0; k < m; ++k) {\n                    if (k != j) { A[i][j].a[k][k] = 1; continue; }\n                    for (int l = 0; l <= m; ++l) A[i][j].a[k][l] = 1;\n                }\n            }\n        } else {\n            for (int j = 0; j < m; ++j) {\n                if (j == 0) A[i][j] = S[i-1][0];\n                else A[i][j] = S[i-1][j] * P[i-1][j-1];\n            }\n        }\n        P[i][0] = A[i][0];\n        for (int j = 1; j < m; ++j) P[i][j] = P[i][j-1] * A[i][j];\n        S[i][m-1] = A[i][m-1];\n        for (int j = m-2; j >= 0; --j) S[i][j] = A[i][j] * S[i][j+1];\n    }\n    int cur = 0;\n    for (int i = len-1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        ll cnt = bin[i];\n        while (cnt--) {\n            ans = ans * A[i][cur];\n            cur = (cur + 1) % m;\n        }\n    }\n    cout << ans.a[0][m] << endl;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B, m):\n    size = m + 1\n    C = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for i in range(size):\n        for k in range(size):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik:\n                for j in range(size):\n                    C[i][j] = (C[i][j] + aik * B[k][j]) % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef copy_mat(mat):\n    return [row[:] for row in mat]\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n\n    # compute base-m digits of n\n    bin_digits = []\n    tmp = n\n    while tmp:\n        bin_digits.append(tmp % m)\n        tmp //= m\n    if not bin_digits:\n        bin_digits = [0]\n    L = len(bin_digits)\n\n    # initialize ans as a row vector (matrix with first row all ones)\n    size = m + 1\n    ans = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for j in range(size):\n        ans[0][j] = 1\n\n    # arrays of matrices: A, P, S for each digit position\n    A = [None] * L\n    P = [None] * L\n    S = [None] * L\n\n    for i in range(L):\n        A_i = [None] * m\n        if i == 0:\n            for j in range(m):\n                mat = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n                mat[m][m] = 1\n                for k in range(m):\n                    if k != j:\n                        mat[k][k] = 1\n                    else:\n                        for l in range(size):\n                            mat[k][l] = 1\n                A_i[j] = mat\n        else:\n            for j in range(m):\n                if j == 0:\n                    A_i[j] = copy_mat(S[i-1][0])\n                else:\n                    A_i[j] = mat_mul(S[i-1][j], P[i-1][j-1], m)\n        A[i] = A_i\n\n        # compute P[i]\n        P_i = [None] * m\n        P_i[0] = copy_mat(A[i][0])\n        for j in range(1, m):\n            P_i[j] = mat_mul(P_i[j-1], A[i][j], m)\n        P[i] = P_i\n\n        # compute S[i]\n        S_i = [None] * m\n        S_i[m-1] = copy_mat(A[i][m-1])\n        for j in range(m-2, -1, -1):\n            S_i[j] = mat_mul(A[i][j], S_i[j+1], m)\n        S[i] = S_i\n\n    cur = 0\n    for i in range(L-1, -1, -1):\n        cnt = bin_digits[i]\n        while cnt:\n            ans = mat_mul(ans, A[i][cur], m)\n            cur = (cur + 1) % m\n            cnt -= 1\n\n    print(ans[0][m])\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.3351351299206726e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -6.222531374078244e-05, -0.0007587176514789462, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0007195267826318741, -0.011053166352212429, 0.0, 0.0, -3.6954811548639555e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0001820160250645131, -4.291525328881107e-06, -0.012133950367569923, -9.142934868577868e-05, 0.0, -0.00034540885826572776, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -9.619726915843785e-05, -0.005636157002300024, -2.6702524337451905e-05, -1